{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-29T13:51:41.441Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**Summary**\n\nImplemented `CommandError` and switched `status`, `show`, and `report` to throw it, with `runCli` centralizing output and exit-code handling.\n\n**Changed**\n- `src/cli/command-error.ts` (new): `CommandError` with `exitCode` (default 1) and optional `next`.\n- `src/cli/run.ts`: catches `CommandError` → non-empty stderr message, optional `Next:` stdout line, sets `process.exitCode`; `ConfigLoadError` sets exit code 1 instead of `process.exit(1)`.\n- `src/cli/status.ts`, `src/cli/show.ts`, `src/cli/report.ts`: `console.error(...); process.exit(1);` pairs became throws with byte-identical text.\n- `tests/cli-capture.ts` (new): `runCliCaptured` capturing lines/exit code and restoring all globals.\n- `tests/cli-config-errors.test.ts`: `runInProject` now reads `process.exitCode`; titles/assertions unchanged.\n- `tests/command-error.test.ts` (new): coverage for each converted command plus the caller-carries-on path.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/command-error.test.ts` → 5 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full suite, lint) → all green.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/111-commands-throw/.run/results/1.md`."}}
